.TH MORSE 6.SH NAMEmorse \- write text as Morse code.SH SYNOPSIS\fBmorse\fR [\-s] [string ...].SH DESCRIPTION\fBmorse\fR writes its arguments, or its standard input, as Morse code,one letter to a line: in words, as `dit dit dit,', or with \fB\-s\fR indots and dashes, as `...,'.  From 4.3BSD Net/2.